{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You shall not listen to the words of that prophet.</b> Do not turn to his words to see whether there is any substance in any of them, for there is no doubt that all his words are falsehood that he has fabricated entirely to do evil, as it says: כִּי דִבֶּר סָרָה (Deuteronomy 13:6), and the sign or wonder was performed by means of sorcery or trickery and the like — not by the power of prophecy that came upon him." "<b>Or to that dreamer of dreams.</b> To see whether there is any truth in any of his dream, but you shall know without doubt that he did not dream anything of what he said — rather, he fabricated it all from his own heart in order to seduce." "<b>For HaShem your Elohim is testing you.</b> For when you regard as an enemy the one who speaks against your Elohim, in this you are tested before Him as His lovers." "<b>To know.</b> So that your love, proven in actuality, may be in actuality before His active knowing, for the good of the world as is fitting, in the matter that is prepared in actuality to receive the influx of His goodness."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:21.323567390Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}